From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0795: the page counts of the upload buffer pools (shared memory, constants, transfer vertices, frame indices) kept in the key file (kind 8) and their pages made and touched at start by the warm-up; the pages made while the game runs are logged

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (hitch work of 2026-11-27, scratch/hitch3/DESIGN.md; extends 0790, 0793 and 0794)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: What is left in the worst frame of the game's first 1080p scene after 0793 / 0794 (53-87 ms, median 81) follows its page
  faults (about 21 ms + 2.1 us each, 11-35 thousand of them: scratch/hitch2/RESULTS.md), and the command processor makes in that frame
  21 shared memory upload pages and 9 (in another run 21) constant buffer pool pages of 2 MiB each: GraphicsUploadBufferPool makes a
  page (CreateCommittedResource upload heap + Map) whenever the pages it has are all in use and the first write to a fresh page faults
  its memory in. A throwaway experiment that made and touched 96 + 48 pages of those two pools at start brought that frame to 40 ms
  with 2 thousand faults (runs h2-x5, h2-x6; the shared memory pool alone was not enough: h2-x2, h2-x3: 52-69 ms), for 46-54 ms of
  boot; the page log of a run without it (h2-x4, a two minute drive) shows the pools end with 34 / 12 / 2 / 0 pages (shared memory,
  constants, transfer vertices, frame indices): 13 / 3 / 1 of them made by 5.2 s (the first engine frame), 21 / 9 in the first 1080p
  scene (15.9 s), 1 transfer vertex page at 22.6 s, none after; about two thirds of what the experiment made were never needed.
  Nothing frees a pool's pages while the game runs (the destructor and ClearCache are the only ways; ClearCache is reached only
  through D3D12CommandProcessor::ClearCaches, which nothing calls; render_target_trim_seconds and the texture cache's limits do not
  touch the pools), so a page made at start is reused. This keeps the count of each pool in
  0790's key file: kind 8, key = pool id << 24 | pages (0 shared memory, 1 constants, 2 transfer vertices, 3 frame indices),
  appended by D3D12CommandProcessor::RecordUploadPoolHighWater at the end of a frame whenever a pool has more pages than the file
  has for it (the file's largest counts, so it converges over the runs and never needs a rewrite). D3D12CommandProcessor::
  WarmUpHostAllocations makes the missing pages of each pool first, out of the same budget as the other objects (d3d12_warmup_mib, the
  quarter of the video memory left) but at most a quarter of it, with the new GraphicsUploadBufferPool::PreallocatePages: pages
  created and touched (d3d12_warmup_pool_touch: 1 a byte of each 4 KB, the default, 2 the whole page as the experiment did, 0 not;
  d3d12_warmup_pools=false leaves the pools alone, for an A/B in one build) and put at the end of the writable list as never used,
  so the first requests take them in turn and none is made while they last.
  The [warm-up] line gets 'upload pool pages: N (M MiB, X ms, touch mode T): shared memory a, constants b, transfer vertices c,
  frame indices d' at its end (the head counts them too); and a page a pool makes while the game runs is logged with what creating
  it cost ('Upload buffer pool '<name>': page N (2048 KiB) made while the game runs: X us (K so far)', the first 16 of each pool).
  The key file's header is unchanged, so an existing file is kept and gets kind 8 records appended; a reader of this build skips the
  records of kinds 9-63 (a later patch's) and keeps them in the file instead of cutting the file at the first record it does not
  know, as 0790-0794 do (a 0794 build cuts a file that has kind 8 records at the first of them: do not run one on a cache this
  build wrote). Left lazy on purpose: the immediate drawer's pool (the presenter's thread, not in the scene's frame), the readback and
  scratch buffers, descriptor heaps, the textures (see DESIGN.md of the work for each).
  Needs 0790, 0791, 0792, 0760, 0793 and 0794.
Bucket: REDO

0795-upload-pool-warm-up.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, T0/T2).

---
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.h
@@ -743,6 +743,25 @@ class D3D12CommandProcessor : public CommandProcessor {
 
   std::unique_ptr<ui::d3d12::D3D12UploadBufferPool> constant_buffer_pool_;
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the upload buffer pools whose page counts are kept in the key file (kind 8, the id is
+  // part of the key: do not renumber) and made at start by WarmUpHostAllocations. A pool makes a page (2 MB, the frame
+  // index pool's about 12 MB) each time the pages it has are all in use, and keeps it: a drive of two minutes ended
+  // with 34 / 12 / 2 / 0 of them, 21 + 9 of those made in one frame of the game's front end (page faults: about 21 ms
+  // + 2.1 us each).
+  enum UploadPoolId : uint32_t {
+    kUploadPoolSharedMemory = 0,
+    kUploadPoolConstants = 1,
+    kUploadPoolTransferVertices = 2,
+    kUploadPoolFrameIndices = 3,
+    kUploadPoolCount,
+  };
+  ui::d3d12::D3D12UploadBufferPool* GetWarmupUploadPool(uint32_t pool_id) const;
+  static const char* GetWarmupUploadPoolName(uint32_t pool_id);
+  // At the end of a frame: a pool that has more pages than the key file knows of gets its count recorded.
+  void RecordUploadPoolHighWater();
+  // The largest page count of each pool the key file has (and this run recorded).
+  uint32_t upload_pool_pages_recorded_[kUploadPoolCount] = {};
+
   static constexpr uint32_t kViewBindfulHeapSize = 32768;
   static_assert(kViewBindfulHeapSize <= D3D12_MAX_SHADER_VISIBLE_DESCRIPTOR_HEAP_SIZE_TIER_1);
   std::unique_ptr<ui::d3d12::D3D12DescriptorHeapPool> view_bindful_heap_pool_;
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/primitive_processor.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/primitive_processor.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/primitive_processor.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/primitive_processor.h
@@ -35,6 +35,9 @@ class D3D12PrimitiveProcessor final : public PrimitiveProcessor {
   bool Initialize();
   void Shutdown(bool from_destructor = false);
   void ClearCache() { frame_index_buffer_pool_->ClearCache(); }
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the pool of the converted index buffers (pages of about 12 MB), for
+  // D3D12CommandProcessor to keep its page count and make its pages at start.
+  ui::d3d12::D3D12UploadBufferPool* GetFrameIndexBufferPool() const { return frame_index_buffer_pool_.get(); }
 
   void CompletedSubmissionUpdated();
   void BeginSubmission();
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/render_target_cache.h
@@ -80,6 +80,11 @@ class D3D12RenderTargetCache final : public RenderTargetCache {
   static constexpr uint32_t kWarmupKindRenderTarget = 5;
   static constexpr uint32_t kWarmupKindSharedMemoryWindow = 6;
   static constexpr uint32_t kWarmupKindScaledResolveHeap = 7;
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): kind 8 is the page count a run's upload buffer pool reached (pool id << 24 | pages; the
+  // pool ids are D3D12CommandProcessor's); the file keeps the largest of each pool, so the pools make that many pages
+  // at start. The kinds from 9 to 63 are left for later: a reader of this kind keeps what it doesn't know in the file
+  // (an older one stops reading at the first record it doesn't know and cuts the file there).
+  static constexpr uint32_t kWarmupKindUploadPoolPages = 8;
   // For the shared memory and the texture cache, which make the other two kinds, through the command processor.
   void RecordWarmupKey(uint32_t kind, uint32_t key) { RecordRuntimePipelineKey(kind, key); }
   // The records of the three kinds in the file, in the order the earlier runs made them in (and so needed them in);
@@ -89,6 +94,11 @@ class D3D12RenderTargetCache final : public RenderTargetCache {
   uint64_t EstimateWarmupRenderTargetBytes(uint32_t key_value) const;
   // Makes the render target of the key now (see RenderTargetCache::PrecreateRenderTarget).
   bool WarmUpRenderTarget(uint32_t key_value, uint64_t& host_memory_bytes_out);
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the pool of the transfer and clear quads' vertices (null on the paths that make no
+  // transfers).
+  ui::d3d12::D3D12UploadBufferPool* GetTransferVertexBufferPool() const {
+    return transfer_vertex_buffer_pool_.get();
+  }
 
   void CompletedSubmissionUpdated();
   void BeginSubmission();
@@ -859,9 +869,13 @@ class D3D12RenderTargetCache final : public RenderTargetCache {
     kRuntimePipelineKeyRenderTarget = kWarmupKindRenderTarget,
     kRuntimePipelineKeySharedMemoryWindow = kWarmupKindSharedMemoryWindow,
     kRuntimePipelineKeyScaledResolveHeap = kWarmupKindScaledResolveHeap,
-    kRuntimePipelineKeyLast = kRuntimePipelineKeyScaledResolveHeap,
+    kRuntimePipelineKeyUploadPoolPages = kWarmupKindUploadPoolPages,  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795)
+    kRuntimePipelineKeyLast = kRuntimePipelineKeyUploadPoolPages,
+    // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): a record of a kind above Last and up to this is a later patch's: skipped, and kept in
+    // the file. Beyond it, or kind 0, the file is taken as corrupted from there on, as before.
+    kRuntimePipelineKeyKnownLimit = 63,
   };
-  // The records of kinds 5 to 7 read from the file, until TakeWarmupRecords.
+  // The records of kinds 5 to 8 read from the file, until TakeWarmupRecords.
   std::vector<uint64_t> warmup_records_;
   // Appends the key to the file (and flushes: a few dozen records a run, and the process ends with _Exit) unless it
   // is already there or the keys are being made from the file.
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/shared_memory.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/shared_memory.h
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/shared_memory.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/shared_memory.h
@@ -129,6 +129,9 @@ class D3D12SharedMemory : public SharedMemory {
   uint32_t GetSparseAllocationGranularityLog2() const { return host_gpu_memory_sparse_granularity_log2(); }
   // Makes the heaps behind the range now, at start (EnsureRangeAllocated; not logged as a run-time creation).
   bool WarmUpHostGpuMemory(uint32_t start, uint32_t length);
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the pool of the 2 MB upload pages (the memory the guest's data is copied through to
+  // the shared memory), for D3D12CommandProcessor to keep its page count and make its pages at start.
+  ui::d3d12::D3D12UploadBufferPool* GetUploadBufferPool() const { return upload_buffer_pool_.get(); }
 
  protected:
   bool AllocateSparseHostGpuMemoryRange(uint32_t offset_allocations,
diff --git a/include/rex/ui/d3d12/d3d12_upload_buffer_pool.h b/include/rex/ui/d3d12/d3d12_upload_buffer_pool.h
--- a/include/rex/ui/d3d12/d3d12_upload_buffer_pool.h
+++ b/include/rex/ui/d3d12/d3d12_upload_buffer_pool.h
@@ -27,8 +27,15 @@ class D3D12UploadBufferPool : public GraphicsUploadBufferPool {
                           ID3D12Resource** buffer_out, size_t* offset_out, size_t* size_out,
                           D3D12_GPU_VIRTUAL_ADDRESS* gpu_address_out);
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): what the pool is called in the log (the pages it makes while the game runs are logged,
+  // with what creating them cost, the first few of each pool). The string must outlive the pool.
+  void SetName(const char* name) { name_ = name; }
+
  protected:
   Page* CreatePageImplementation() override;
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): touch_mode 1 writes a byte to each 4 KB of the page's memory, 2 writes the whole page,
+  // 0 nothing.
+  void TouchPageImplementation(Page* page, uint32_t touch_mode) override;
 
  private:
   struct D3D12Page : public Page {
@@ -41,6 +48,10 @@ class D3D12UploadBufferPool : public GraphicsUploadBufferPool {
   };
 
   const D3D12Provider& provider_;
+
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795)
+  const char* name_ = nullptr;
+  uint32_t runtime_pages_logged_ = 0;
 };
 
 }  // namespace rex::ui::d3d12
diff --git a/include/rex/ui/graphics_upload_buffer_pool.h b/include/rex/ui/graphics_upload_buffer_pool.h
--- a/include/rex/ui/graphics_upload_buffer_pool.h
+++ b/include/rex/ui/graphics_upload_buffer_pool.h
@@ -39,6 +39,17 @@ class GraphicsUploadBufferPool {
   // implementation doesn't require explicit flushing.
   void FlushWrites();
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the pages made so far - they are only deleted by ClearCache, which is not called while
+  // the game runs, so this is the high-water mark of the pages the requests needed at once - and the size of one.
+  size_t GetPageCount() const { return page_count_; }
+  size_t GetPageSize() const { return page_size_; }
+  // Makes pages now, until the pool has `count` in all, and puts them on the end of the writable list as pages never
+  // used (the requests take the pages of that list in turn, so none is made on a request while they last), after the
+  // implementation touched each of them (TouchPageImplementation, touch_mode is its business), so that what the first
+  // use of a fresh page costs - the memory's page faults - is paid here and not in a frame. Returns the number of pages
+  // the pool has afterwards (less than count if creating one failed). Call it on the thread that uses the pool.
+  size_t PreallocatePages(size_t count, uint32_t touch_mode);
+
  protected:
   // Extended by the implementation.
   struct Page {
@@ -60,6 +71,9 @@ class GraphicsUploadBufferPool {
 
   virtual void FlushPageWrites(Page* page, size_t offset, size_t size);
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): writes to the page's memory so it is paged in (does nothing by default).
+  virtual void TouchPageImplementation(Page* page, uint32_t touch_mode);
+
   // May be increased by the implementation on creation or on first allocation
   // to avoid wasting space if the real allocation turns out to be bigger than
   // the specified page size.
@@ -76,6 +90,11 @@ class GraphicsUploadBufferPool {
 
   size_t current_page_used_ = 0;
   size_t current_page_flushed_ = 0;
+
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the pages in the lists above; and whether PreallocatePages is making pages (so an
+  // implementation can tell those from the ones a request makes in the middle of a frame).
+  size_t page_count_ = 0;
+  bool preallocating_ = false;
 };
 
 }  // namespace ui
diff --git a/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp b/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
--- a/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/d3d12/command_processor.cpp
@@ -109,6 +109,19 @@ REXCVAR_DEFINE_UINT32(d3d12_warmup_mib, 0, "GPU/D3D12",
                       "of the game's first minutes need about 600 MiB at scale 1)")
     .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kRequiresRestart);
 
+// LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the upload buffer pools' pages made at start by the warm-up.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(d3d12_warmup_pools, true, "GPU/D3D12",
+                    "With d3d12_warmup, also make (and touch) the pages of the upload buffer pools (shared memory uploads, "
+                    "constants, transfer vertices, frame indices) that the earlier runs needed, from the page counts in "
+                    "<title>.rtv.d3d12.xrtp; off: the pools make their pages when they run out, as before (the counts are "
+                    "still kept)")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kRequiresRestart);
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_UINT32(d3d12_warmup_pool_touch, 1, "GPU/D3D12",
+                      "How d3d12_warmup touches the upload buffer pool pages it makes, so their memory is paged in at "
+                      "start and not in the frame that first writes them: 1 a byte of each 4 KB, 2 the whole page (what "
+                      "the experiment before it did), 0 not at all (the pages exist, the page faults come in the frame)")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kRequiresRestart);
+
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, gpu_regwrite_bulk);
 REXCVAR_DECLARE(bool, gpu_batch_perf_counters);
 // HDR output's trims (defined in graphics/command_processor.cpp).
@@ -506,6 +519,26 @@ void D3D12CommandProcessor::WarmUpHostAllocations() {
     return;
   }
   std::vector<uint64_t> records = render_target_cache_->TakeWarmupRecords();
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the page count of each upload pool in the key file (the largest of its kind 8 records),
+  // kept also with the warm-up off: a pool that grows beyond it is what the run then records. The pools are named for
+  // the log of the pages they make while the game runs.
+  uint32_t pool_pages_stored[kUploadPoolCount] = {};
+  for (uint32_t pool_id = 0; pool_id < kUploadPoolCount; ++pool_id) {
+    if (ui::d3d12::D3D12UploadBufferPool* pool = GetWarmupUploadPool(pool_id)) {
+      pool->SetName(GetWarmupUploadPoolName(pool_id));
+    }
+  }
+  for (const uint64_t record : records) {
+    if (uint32_t(record >> 32) == D3D12RenderTargetCache::kWarmupKindUploadPoolPages) {
+      const uint32_t pool_id = uint32_t(record) >> 24;
+      if (pool_id < kUploadPoolCount) {
+        pool_pages_stored[pool_id] = std::max(pool_pages_stored[pool_id], uint32_t(record) & 0xFFFFFF);
+      }
+    }
+  }
+  for (uint32_t pool_id = 0; pool_id < kUploadPoolCount; ++pool_id) {
+    upload_pool_pages_recorded_[pool_id] = pool_pages_stored[pool_id];
+  }
   if (!REXCVAR_GET(d3d12_warmup)) {
     return;
   }
@@ -535,14 +568,40 @@ void D3D12CommandProcessor::WarmUpHostAllocations() {
   const uint32_t window_log2 = shared_memory_->GetSparseAllocationGranularityLog2();
   const uint64_t scaled_heap_bytes = D3D12TextureCache::GetScaledResolveHeapBytes();
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the upload pools' pages go first, out of the same budget, but at most a quarter of it: a
+  // page saves the most hitch for its size (its first touch is about 512 page faults of 4 KB, ~1 ms in a frame at
+  // 2.1 us each, against 0.2-0.6 ms at start), and there are few of them (34 + 12 + 2 pages of 2 MB for a drive of two
+  // minutes).
+  uint32_t pool_pages_to_make[kUploadPoolCount] = {};
+  uint64_t pool_page_bytes[kUploadPoolCount] = {};
+  size_t pool_pages_over_budget = 0;
+  uint64_t pools_spent = 0;
+  const bool pools_wanted = REXCVAR_GET(d3d12_warmup_pools);
+  for (uint32_t pool_id = 0; pool_id < kUploadPoolCount; ++pool_id) {
+    ui::d3d12::D3D12UploadBufferPool* pool = GetWarmupUploadPool(pool_id);
+    if (!pools_wanted || !pool || pool_pages_stored[pool_id] <= pool->GetPageCount()) {
+      continue;
+    }
+    pool_page_bytes[pool_id] = pool->GetPageSize();
+    const uint64_t missing = pool_pages_stored[pool_id] - pool->GetPageCount();
+    const uint64_t pools_cap = budget_bytes / 4;
+    const uint64_t room = pools_cap > pools_spent ? (pools_cap - pools_spent) / pool_page_bytes[pool_id] : 0;
+    pool_pages_to_make[pool_id] = uint32_t(std::min(missing, room));
+    pool_pages_over_budget += size_t(missing - pool_pages_to_make[pool_id]);
+    pools_spent += uint64_t(pool_pages_to_make[pool_id]) * pool_page_bytes[pool_id];
+  }
+
   // Choose, in the order of the file (the order the objects were first needed in), what fits the budget.
   std::vector<uint32_t> windows, heaps, render_targets;
-  uint64_t spent = 0;
+  uint64_t spent = pools_spent;
   size_t over_budget = 0, not_for_this_run = 0;
   for (const uint64_t record : records) {
     const uint32_t kind = uint32_t(record >> 32);
     const uint32_t key = uint32_t(record);
     uint64_t bytes = 0;
+    if (kind == D3D12RenderTargetCache::kWarmupKindUploadPoolPages) {
+      continue;  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): done above
+    }
     if (kind == D3D12RenderTargetCache::kWarmupKindSharedMemoryWindow) {
       if (window_log2 != UINT32_MAX && (key >> 24) == window_log2 &&
           (uint64_t(key & 0xFFFFFF) << window_log2) < SharedMemory::kBufferSize) {
@@ -580,6 +639,24 @@ void D3D12CommandProcessor::WarmUpHostAllocations() {
   };
   size_t failed = 0;
 
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the upload pools' pages (made and touched), chosen above.
+  size_t pool_pages_made[kUploadPoolCount] = {};
+  uint64_t pool_pages_bytes = 0;
+  const auto pools_start = Clock::now();
+  const uint32_t pool_touch = REXCVAR_GET(d3d12_warmup_pool_touch);
+  for (uint32_t pool_id = 0; pool_id < kUploadPoolCount; ++pool_id) {
+    if (!pool_pages_to_make[pool_id]) {
+      continue;
+    }
+    ui::d3d12::D3D12UploadBufferPool* pool = GetWarmupUploadPool(pool_id);
+    const size_t pages_before = pool->GetPageCount();
+    const size_t pages_after = pool->PreallocatePages(pages_before + pool_pages_to_make[pool_id], pool_touch);
+    pool_pages_made[pool_id] = pages_after - pages_before;
+    pool_pages_bytes += uint64_t(pool_pages_made[pool_id]) * pool_page_bytes[pool_id];
+    failed += pool_pages_to_make[pool_id] - pool_pages_made[pool_id];
+  }
+  const double pools_ms = milliseconds_since(pools_start);
+
   // The shared memory's tile heaps: neighbours together, a heap for each run of at most 8 windows (32 MB).
   size_t windows_made = 0;
   const auto windows_start = Clock::now();
@@ -628,15 +705,83 @@ void D3D12CommandProcessor::WarmUpHostAllocations() {
 
   const uint64_t windows_bytes = window_log2 != UINT32_MAX ? uint64_t(windows_made) << window_log2 : 0;
   const uint64_t heaps_bytes = uint64_t(heaps_made) * scaled_heap_bytes;
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0795): the pool pages, per pool, at the end of the line (the head counts them too: the
+  // allocations, the MiB and the time are everything the warm-up made).
+  size_t pool_pages_made_total = 0;
+  size_t pool_pages_stored_total = 0;
+  for (uint32_t pool_id = 0; pool_id < kUploadPoolCount; ++pool_id) {
+    pool_pages_made_total += pool_pages_made[pool_id];
+    pool_pages_stored_total += pool_pages_stored[pool_id];
+  }
+  const std::string pool_pages_notes =
+      std::string(!pools_wanted ? " (off: d3d12_warmup_pools=false)"
+                  : pool_pages_stored_total ? ""
+                                            : " (none stored in the key file yet: this run records them)") +
+      (pool_pages_over_budget
+           ? fmt::format(", {} more left to the first use (over a quarter of the budget)", pool_pages_over_budget)
+           : std::string());
   REXGPU_INFO(
       "[warm-up] {} host allocations ({} MiB) made in {:.1f} ms from the key file: {} shared memory tile heap windows "
       "({} MiB, {:.1f} ms), {} scaled resolve tile heaps ({} MiB, {:.1f} ms), {} render targets ({} MiB, {:.1f} ms); "
-      "left to the first use: {} over the {} MiB budget{}, {} that this run's layout can't ask for, {} that failed",
-      windows_made + heaps_made + render_targets_made,
-      (windows_bytes + heaps_bytes + render_target_bytes) >> 20, milliseconds_since(start), windows_made,
-      windows_bytes >> 20, windows_ms, heaps_made, heaps_bytes >> 20, heaps_ms, render_targets_made,
+      "left to the first use: {} over the {} MiB budget{}, {} that this run's layout can't ask for, {} that failed; "
+      "upload pool pages: {} ({} MiB, {:.1f} ms, touch mode {}): shared memory {}, constants {}, transfer vertices {}, "
+      "frame indices {}{}",
+      windows_made + heaps_made + render_targets_made + pool_pages_made_total,
+      (windows_bytes + heaps_bytes + render_target_bytes + pool_pages_bytes) >> 20, milliseconds_since(start),
+      windows_made, windows_bytes >> 20, windows_ms, heaps_made, heaps_bytes >> 20, heaps_ms, render_targets_made,
       render_target_bytes >> 20, render_targets_ms, over_budget, budget_bytes >> 20,
-      budget_capped ? " (a quarter of the video memory left)" : "", not_for_this_run, failed);
+      budget_capped ? " (a quarter of the video memory left)" : "", not_for_this_run, failed, pool_pages_made_total,
+      pool_pages_bytes >> 20, pools_ms, pool_touch, pool_pages_made[kUploadPoolSharedMemory],
+      pool_pages_made[kUploadPoolConstants], pool_pages_made[kUploadPoolTransferVertices],
+      pool_pages_made[kUploadPoolFrameIndices], pool_pages_notes);
+}
